==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets two distinct Operations share a single AuditEntry, breaking the append-only / immutability invariant on audit_entries.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOnlySharedWith  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OwnerOnlySharedWith.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a non-owner caller succeed at PATCHing shared_with, which is the exact owner-only-share-control violation FR-010/SC-011 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SharedWithSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_SharedWithSameTeam.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a task carry a sharee from a different team, the exact cross-team-sharing case FR-012 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NoCrossTeamSharing
      - FR_012_NoCrossTeamSharing: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_GetTaskAccessRule  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_GetTaskAccessRule.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets an in-team non-owner non-sharee non-admin caller successfully GET a task — the in-team-no-rel leak FR-004 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_InTeamNoRelBlocked
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_InTeamNoRelBlocked: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeleteAccessRule  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_DeleteAccessRule.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a sharee successfully DELETE a task, which is the Q3=B / FR-011 violation.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ShareeNoDelete
      - FR_011_ShareeNoDelete: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a caller in team A succeed at PATCHing fields of a task in team B — the cross-team leakage FR-014/SC-003 makes impossible.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_CrossTeamBlocked, FR_014_CrossTeamByteEquiv
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamBlocked: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_CrossTeamByteEquiv: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditPerMutation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditPerMutation.als
    rationale: removing this fact lets a successful task mutation slip through without producing any audit entry — exactly the state-change-without-audit case FR-015/SC-007 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_NoOrphanAudit, FR_018_AuditAtomicity
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_NoOrphanAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditAtomicity: FAIL (expected)

